# Analects Book 19 (子張) — draft, first part: lemmata 0–19 = passages 19.1–19.19 (UNITS_A[0] is lemma 0).
# Same format as the pilot (drafts/analects-01/units.py) and Book 18. Token format as the pilot:
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every bound compound and every character not yet in the glossary (on every occurrence).
# Passages follow Zhu Xi's chapter breaks (heading: 此篇皆記弟子之言而子夏為多子貢次之…凡二十五章; each ○ checked
# in the commentary file KR1h0015_009.txt): 19.1 = unit 0, 19.2 = 1, 19.3 = 2, 19.4 = 3, 19.5 = 4, 19.6 = 5,
# 19.7 = 6, 19.8 = 7, 19.9 = 8, 19.10 = 9, 19.11 = 10, 19.12 = 11–12 (Ziyou's charge, then Zixia's answer after
# Zhu Xi's comment), 19.13 = 13, 19.14 = 14, 19.15 = 15, 19.16 = 16, 19.17 = 17, 19.18 = 18, 19.19 = 19.
# Each stretch holds at most one chapter (no npas).
# Line breaks: the lines of t (one more than the ^ breaks after the first token) equal the lines of l in
# every unit. Speech openers (子張曰：「, 子夏曰：「 …) stand on a line of their own when the speech runs to more
# than one line (as Book 18). Quotation marks balance within every unit. Quote inside a quote: 『』 in w, ‘’
# in l and i (unit 2, the disciples citing Zixia). 吾聞諸夫子 (units 17, 18) is followed by a colon, not an
# inner quote: there is no 曰, and the words are Master Zeng's report of the Master's sense.
# Cross-references cite the shipped passage numbers: 見危授命 (14.13) and 見得思義 (16.10) for 19.1; 𢎞 'broad'
#   (8.7); 損友 (16.4); 異端 (2.16); 好學…也已 (1.14); 博學 (6.25, 12.15, 9.2); 在其中矣 (2.18, 15.31); 致其身
