dict(pas="19.3", w="子夏=zǐ xià/Zixia | 之/'s | 門人=mén rén/disciples | 問/asked | 交/(about) dealing with others | 於/of | 子張。=zǐ zhāng/Zizhang | ^子張=zǐ zhāng/Zizhang | 曰：「/said | 子夏=zǐ xià/Zixia | 云/says | 何？」/what | ^對/(they) answered | 曰：「/saying | 子夏=zǐ xià/Zixia | 曰：『/says | 可/acceptable | 者/those who are | 與=yǔ/keep company with | 之，/them | 其/(and) the | 不/not | 可/acceptable | 者/ones | 拒=jù/turn away | 之。』」/them | ^子張=zǐ zhāng/Zizhang | 曰：「/said | ^異/(it) differs | 乎/from | 吾/what I | 所/(that which) | 聞：/have heard | ^君子=jūn zǐ/the gentleman | 尊=zūn/honours | 賢/the worthy | 而/and | 容/has room for | 衆，/the many | 嘉=jiā/praises | 善/the good | 而/and | 矜=jīn/pities | 不/(those) not | 能。/able | ^我/I | 之/(makes the clause a noun) | 大/greatly | 賢/worthy | 與，=yú/(am I?) | 於/among | 人/others | 何/what (one) | 所/(is there that) | 不/(I would) not | 容？/have room for | ^我/I | 之/(makes the clause a noun) | 不/not | 賢/worthy | 與，=yú/(am I?) | 人/others | 將=jiāng/will | 拒=jù/turn away | 我，/me | 如之何=rú zhī hé/how | 其/(could I) | 拒=jù/turn away | 人/others | 也？」/(final)",
  l="Zixia's disciples asked Zizhang about dealing with others.\nZizhang said: “What does Zixia say?”\nThey answered: “Zixia says: ‘Those who are acceptable, keep company with; those who are not acceptable, turn away.’”\nZizhang said:\n“That differs from what I have heard:\nthe gentleman honours the worthy and has room for the many; he praises the good and pities those who are not able.\nAm I greatly worthy? Then among others whom would I not have room for?\nAm I not worthy? Others will turn me away — how could I be the one to turn others away?”",
  i="Zixia's disciples asked Zizhang how one should deal with other people. “What does Zixia tell you?” said Zizhang. They answered: “Zixia says: ‘Keep company with those who are fit for it, and turn away those who are not.’” Zizhang said: “That is not what I was taught. A gentleman honours men of worth and makes room for everyone; he commends the good and feels for those who fall short. If I am a man of great worth, is there anyone I could not make room for? If I am not, others will turn me away — how would I come to be turning them away?”",
  n="子夏 Zixia is the disciple Bu Shang 卜商 (1.7). 交 'dealing with others, association' — Kong Anguo in He Yan: they asked about the way of dealing with people (與人交接之道也). 云 'to say'. 可者 'those who are acceptable', 者 making a noun of 可; 與 yǔ 'to keep company with'. 拒 jù 'to turn away, to refuse'. 異乎 'differs from' (乎 = 於). 尊 'to honour'; 容 'to have room for, to tolerate'; 嘉 'to praise'; 矜 jīn 'to pity, to feel for'; 不能 'those who are not able'. In 我之大賢與, 之 between subject and predicate turns 'I am greatly worthy' into a phrase, and 與 yú puts it as a question (Zhu Xi: 賢與之與平聲): 'am I greatly worthy?' — each question then works as an 'if'. 如之何其拒人也 'how could it be that I turn others away?': 如之何 'how' (2.20), 其 'could (I)'. Zhu Xi: Zixia's words are cramped and narrow, and Zizhang is right to mock them (子夏之言廹狹子張譏之是也); but what Zizhang says has the fault of aiming too high (亦有過髙之弊): a man of great worth has room for all, yet must still break with grave wrongdoing (然大故亦所當絶); one not worthy may not turn people away, yet harmful friends (損友, 16.4) should still be kept at a distance (然損友亦所當逺); the learner must weigh this. Bao Xian in He Yan reconciles the two: in friendship one should go by Zixia, in general dealings by Zizhang (友交當如子夏汎交當如子張也). Variants: He Yan's text writes 距 for 拒 (the older loan form, the same word), reads 異乎吾所聞也 with a final 也, and 我大賢與, 我不賢與 without 之."),
